tiltxcorr Version 5.2.17 Sep 19 2026 00:48:39
Copyright (C) 1994-2025 by the Regents of the University of Colorado
Usage: tiltxcorr [Options] input_file output_file
Options can be abbreviated, current short name abbreviations are in parentheses
Options:

Input and Output Specification
 -input (-inp)  OR  -InputFile   File
    Input image file
 -piece (-pie)  OR  -PieceListFile   File
    Piece file with rearranged Z values
 -reference (-ref)  OR  -ReferenceFile   File
    Input file containing an image to use as a reference
 -rview (-rv)  OR  -ReferenceView   Int
    View number of image to use in reference file
 -output (-ou)  OR  -OutputFile   File
    Output file for transforms or for patch tracking model
 -rotation (-ro)  OR  -RotationAngle   Float
    Rotation angle from the Y axis to the tilt axis
 -first (-f)  OR  -FirstTiltAngle   Float
    Tilt angle of first view in degrees
 -increment (-inc)  OR  -TiltIncrement   Float
    Increment between tilt angles
 -tiltfile (-ti)  OR  -TiltFile   File
    File with tilt angles
 -angles (-ang)  OR  -TiltAngles   Floats
    Individual tilt angles for each view
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -offset (-of)  OR  -AngleOffset   Float
    Amount to add to all entered tilt angles
 -reverse (-rev)  OR  -ReverseOrder
    Reverse order of processing when all views have same tilt angle
 -prexf (-pre)  OR  -PrealignmentTransformFile   File
    File with transforms used to align images for patch tracking
 -imagebinned (-im)  OR  -ImagesAreBinned   Int
    The current binning of the images relative to raw stack
 -pixel (-pix)  OR  -PixelSize   Float
    Pixel size of unbinned images in nanometers
 -unali (-un)  OR  -UnalignedSizeXandY   2 ints
    Size of unaligned stack in X and Y

General Options Preparing for Correlations
 -binning (-bi)  OR  -BinningToApply   Int
    Binning or other reduction to apply to the trimmed, padded images
 -antialias (-ant)  OR  -AntialiasFilter   Int
    Type of antialiasing filter to reduce images with instead of binning
 -radius1  OR  -FilterRadius1   Float
    Left cutoff radius for filter
 -radius2  OR  -FilterRadius2   Float
    Right cutoff radius for filter, in binned reciprocal pixels
 -nmrad2 (-nmr)  OR  -Radius2InvNanometers   Float
    Right cutoff frequency for filter as periodicity in nm
 -sigma1  OR  -FilterSigma1   Float
    Sigma for low-frequency inverted Gaussian filter, in binned 1/pixels
 -nmsig1  OR  -Sigma1InvNanometers   Float
    Sigma for low-frequency inverted Gaussian filter as periodicity in 1/nm
 -sigma2  OR  -FilterSigma2   Float
    Sigma for Gaussian rolloff below radius1 and above radius2 in 1/pixel
 -nmsig2  OR  -Sigma2InvNanometers   Float
    Sigma for Gaussian rolloff below radius1 and above radius2 in 1/nm
 -border (-bor)  OR  -BordersInXandY   2 ints
    Number of pixels to trim off each edge in X and in Y
 -ubborder (-ubb)  OR  -UnbinnedBordersXY   2 ints
    Amount to trim off each edge in X and Y, in unbinned pixels of raw stack.
 -xminmax (-x)  OR  -XMinAndMax   2 ints
    Starting and ending coordinates to correlate in X (overrides X border)
 -yminmax (-y)  OR  -YMinAndMax   2 ints
    Starting and ending coordinates to correlate in Y (overrides Y border)
 -ubxmm (-ubx)  OR  -UnbinnedXMinAndMax   2 ints
    Unbinned start and end coordinates to correlate in X (overrides X border)
 -ubymm (-uby)  OR  -UnbinnedYMinAndMax   2 ints
    Unbinned start and end coordinates to correlate in Y (overrides Y border)
 -pad  OR  -PadsInXandY   2 ints
    Number of pixels to pad images on each side in X and in Y
 -taper (-tap)  OR  -TapersInXandY   2 ints
    Number of pixels to taper images in X and in Y

General Cross-correlation Options
 -ccc (-cc)  OR  -CorrelationCoefficient
    Find peak with best normalized cross-correlation coefficient
 -iterate (-it)  OR  -IterateCorrelations   Int
    Number of iterations to reduce interpolation of peak position
 -shift (-sh)  OR  -ShiftLimitsXandY   2 ints
    Limits on distance in X and Y to search for correlation peak
 -axial (-ax)  OR  -AxialShiftLimits   2 ints
    Limits on shift perpendicular and parallel to tilt axis (unbinned)
 -rect (-rec)  OR  -RectangularLimits
    Limit peaks to within a rectangular rather than elliptical area

Options for Specifying Subsets of Views or Area
 -boundary (-bou)  OR  -BoundaryModel   File
    Model file with boundary contours around areas to correlate
 -objbound (-objb)  OR  -BoundaryObject   Int
    Object number to use from boundary model; default is all closed objects
 -skip (-sk)  OR  -SkipViews   List
    List of views to skip, aligning across skipped views (ranges OK)
 -break (-br)  OR  -BreakAtViews   List
    List of views to break alignment at (ranges OK)
 -views (-vi)  OR  -StartingEndingViews   2 ints
    Starting and ending view numbers for doing a subset of views

Whole-image Correlation Options
 -exclude (-exc)  OR  -ExcludeCentralPeak
    Exclude central correlation peak due to fixed pattern noise
 -central (-ce)  OR  -CentralPeakExclusionCriteria   3 floats
    Three criterion values controlling exclusion of a peak at (0, 0)
 -leaveaxis (-lea)  OR  -LeaveTiltAxisShifted
    Do not adjust tilt axis back to center if correlated box is not centered
 -cumulative (-cu)  OR  -CumulativeCorrelation
    Add up previously aligned pictures as reference for next alignment
 -absstretch (-ab)  OR  -AbsoluteCosineStretch
    Cosine stretch each image added into the cumulative sum
 -nostretch (-no)  OR  -NoCosineStretch
    Do not do any cosine stretching for correlations or for accumulating into
    the reference (overrides -absstretch)
 -search (-sea)  OR  -SearchMagChanges
    Search for magnification (size) changes
 -changes (-ch)  OR  -ViewsWithMagChanges   List
    List of views at which to search for size changes (default is all)
 -mag (-m)  OR  -MagnificationLimits   2 floats
    Lower and upper limits for size change (default 0.9,1.1)
 -scan (-sca)  OR  -ScanRotationMaxAndStep   2 floats
    Maximum angle and step size to scan for best rotation, or one angle and 0
 -second (-sec)  OR  -SecondPeakBoxSize   2 ints
    Report on second peak if within box of given length and width

Options for Patch-based Correlations
 -size (-siz)  OR  -SizeOfPatchesXandY   2 ints
    Size in X and Y of patches to track by correlation
 -ubsize (-ubs)  OR  -UnbinnedPatchSizeXY   2 ints
    Size in X and Y of patches to track, in unbinned pixels of raw stack
 -varying (-vary)  OR  -VaryingToPatchSizeXY   2 ints
    Set patch positions as if size was given value, in unbinned pixels
 -number (-nu)  OR  -NumberOfPatchesXandY   2 ints
    Number of patches in X and Y to track by correlation
 -overlap (-ov)  OR  -OverlapOfPatchesXandY   2 ints
    Fractional overlap in X and Y between patches (default 0.33, 0.33)
 -seed (-see)  OR  -SeedModel   File
    Input model file with center points to track by correlation
 -objseed (-objs)  OR  -SeedObject   Int
    Number of object to use in seed model; default is all scattered objects

Options for Tilt Series Patch Tracking
 -length (-len)  OR  -LengthAndOverlap   2 ints
    Contour length and minimum overlap for breaking contour into pieces
 -struct (-st)  OR  -MinStructureModeFrac   Float
    Drop patches with a structure measure less than this fraction of the mode
 -elim (-el)  OR  -MaxFracOfPatchesToElim   Float
    Maximum fraction of patches to drop because of low structure measure
 -expand (-exp)  OR  -MaxPatchExpansions   2 floats
    Maximum amounts to expand patches at starting and higher tilts
 -percentile (-pe)  OR  -PercentileToMatch   Float
    Percentile point of summed structure measure to match when expanding
    patches
 -drop (-dr)  OR  -TiltedExpandDropFrac   Float
    Fraction of summed structure criterion below which to drop a tilted patch
 -target (-tar)  OR  -TargetPixelMinAndMax   2 floats
    Min and max pixel sizes to reduce images to for structure analysis
 -variation (-vari)  OR  -FractionOfMaxVariation   Float
    Use a reduction that gives this fraction of maximum variation among
    patches
 -scurve (-scu)  OR  -SigmoidPowerAndHalfRise   2 floats
    Exponent to apply and half-rise point for scaling SD values
 -box  OR  -SdReducedBoxSize   Int
    Box size for measuring local SD in reduced image
 -sdbin (-sd)  OR  -SdBinList   List
    List of reductions at which to compute local SDs
 -domains (-do)  OR  -LocalDomainSizesXandY   2 ints
    Number of local patches in X and Y for fitting to predicted positions
 -prob (-pro)  OR  -CriterionProbabilities   2 floats
    Probabilities controlling outlier elimination

Warping and Miscellaneous options
 -warp (-w)  OR  -FindWarpTransforms   Int
    Use patch correlations to find and save warping transformations
 -pair (-pai)  OR  -RawAndAlignedPair   2 ints
    View # being aligned and total # of views for finding warp between aligned
    and raw image
 -append (-ap)  OR  -AppendToWarpFile
    Add warp transform from pair to an existing output file
 -gpu (-g)  OR  -UseGPU   Int
    Use GPU for computation; 0 for best available one or number of GPU
 -action (-ac)  OR  -ActionIfGPUFails   2 ints
    0 for no action, 1 for warning, 2 for error if GPU cannot be used
 -test (-te)  OR  -TestOutput   File
    File to save processed images and correlations into
 -single (-sin)  OR  -SingleTestPatch   Int
    # of single patch (#'d from 1) for which to save test output
 -verbose (-ve)  OR  -VerboseOutput   Int
    Output diagnostic information at the given level, 1 or 2
 -param (-par)  OR  -ParameterFile   File
    Read parameter entries from file
 -help (-h)  OR  -usage
    Print help output
